  "id": "COMPOUND:31418 - PROTEIN:367",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a complex relationship between Npc189737 and S-methylmethionine--homocysteine S-methyltransferase BHMT2, with multiple pathways converging on the target of Serine--tRNA ligase, cytoplasmic. This enzyme is identified as a target of three distinct compounds: certolizumab pegol, 13-[(2R,3R,4R)-3,4-dihydroxy-2-(hydroxymethyl)-3,4-dihydro-2H-pyrrol-5-yl]-1-hydroxytridecan-5-one, and everolimus. All three compounds are known to interact with BHMT2, indicating that the enzyme may play a role in the metabolic pathways regulated by these drugs. The high scores across the three paths suggest a strong and consistent relationship, possibly reflecting the enzyme's involvement in critical biochemical processes that are targeted by these therapeutic agents. The evidence supports the notion that Npc189737 is likely a regulator or modulator of BHMT2, though further investigation is needed to clarify the exact mechanism of interaction and its functional significance.",
